Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Fast Gates on a Transmon", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A transmon is a superconducting circuit that behaves as a weakly anharmonic \
oscillator. A qubit is stored in its two lowest levels, and a microwave pulse \
at the qubit frequency rotates it between them. The anharmonicity is small, a \
few hundred megahertz against a qubit frequency of several gigahertz, so the \
transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " lies close to the qubit transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 ". A short pulse has a broad spectrum and drives both transitions, carrying \
population out of the qubit. It must also be strong to complete the rotation \
in time. A strong drive couples ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " and pushes the energy of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 ", which moves the qubit transition away from the drive frequency, so the \
rotation misses its target unless the pulse's amplitude and frequency are \
calibrated. A long pulse avoids both problems but is exposed for longer to \
energy decay and dephasing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->329621944,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The gate studied here flips the qubit, taking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ". It rotates the qubit by an angle \[Pi], so it is called a \[Pi] pulse. \
The population a pulse carries out of the qubit, mostly into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ", is called leakage. A correction known as DRAG (derivative removal by \
adiabatic gate) reduces it by adding a second drive to the pulse, shaped so \
that, for a weak drive, the combined pulse has no component at the frequency \
of the transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->515379898,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a given pulse shape, how long the best \[Pi] pulse is, and how much \
DRAG shortens it, has no exact closed-form answer. Both follow from the Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger and Lindblad equations solved with the levels the qubit \
leaks into kept explicitly, and with the amplitude, frequency and DRAG \
coefficient of the pulse calibrated together with its length. For an \
anharmonicity of \[Minus]200 MHz and coherence times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " of 100 \[Mu]s, DRAG lets the pulse shrink until energy decay and dephasing \
alone set its error. Without DRAG the pulse must stay long enough for leakage \
to die out, and its best error is larger."
}], "Text",
 CellID->604760901,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["The Driven Transmon", "Section",
 CellID->1476799103,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["\<\
The transmon is well approximated by an anharmonic oscillator. It is driven \
by a microwave pulse near its qubit frequency, with a DRAG correction added \
to the pulse:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->448336599,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["lab",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "."], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "]", "(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->970785311,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first two terms describe the transmon, and the last term is the drive. \
Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " lowers the number of excitations by one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["q", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " is the qubit frequency and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " is the anharmonicity. For a transmon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " is negative: the transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " lies ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " below the qubit transition."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1377816002,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive oscillates at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 ", detuned from the qubit by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 ", and its envelope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 " sets its strength. The detuning lets the drive follow the qubit \
transition, which a strong drive moves by pushing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " away from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 ". The second term in the bracket is the DRAG correction. It oscillates as \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 " instead of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 ", and its strength follows the slope of the envelope, scaled by the DRAG \
coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 ". Dividing the slope by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " gives it the units of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " is a pure number. For a weak drive and no detuning, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 " removes the component of the drive at the leakage frequency. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " the correction is off and the pulse is a plain microwave drive. The \
amplitude of the envelope, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " are the three controls of the pulse."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1439899046,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive is simplest to describe in a frame rotating with it, which \
subtracts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " for every excitation. In the rotating frame, some drive terms vary only \
with the pulse envelope. Others oscillate at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 ", much faster than the envelope and populations change. These fast terms \
largely average out when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[LessLess]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 "; dropping them is the rotating-wave approximation. What remains is the \
Hamiltonian used throughout:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1641200340,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ")", "-", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "."], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "(", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1424533854,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this frame the first two terms set the energies of the levels, and the \
last two couple neighboring levels. To write these terms as matrices, the \
oscillator is truncated to its five lowest levels, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"4"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 ", which hold the qubit and the levels it leaks into; the last section \
checks that a sixth level does not change the results."
}], "Text",
 CellID->535457321,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell["Define the lowering operator of a five-level oscillator:", "Text",
 CellID->141959522,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "5", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->299517738,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Without detuning, the qubit levels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 " have the same energy in this frame, and the higher levels sit at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"6", 
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2142391071,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"b", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"b", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"b", " ", "@", " ", "b"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
   "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1002769646,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive couples neighboring levels with strengths 1, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox["2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox["3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " and 2:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->436346740,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"b", " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"b", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"",
    "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->2122865143,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coupling between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " is larger than the coupling between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 " by a factor of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox["2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 ", so the drive acts more strongly on the leakage transition than on the \
qubit transition. The leakage transition is also off resonance by only ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 ". Both make leakage easy."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1735808809,ExpressionUUID->"25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],

Cell["The Pulse", "Section",
 CellID->753514147,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The envelope of a pulse of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " must vanish at both ends, so the drive switches on and off smoothly. Its \
slope must vanish there too, so the DRAG correction, which follows the slope, \
also starts and ends at zero. A constant and one cosine harmonic are the \
fewest terms that meet both conditions. They give the raised cosine used here:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1164297175,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   FractionBox["\[Pi]", 
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "(", 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]]}], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->632614636,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It has no shape parameter beyond its amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " and its length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1689610856,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell["Define the envelope:", "Text",
 CellID->1303163127,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"envelope", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"A", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "\[Tau]"}], ")"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
       RowBox[{"t", "/", "\[Tau]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->2098230307,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Without DRAG and detuning, and restricted to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 ", the drive rotates the qubit at the rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ", so the rotation angle is the area under the envelope:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1930159659,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
  RowBox[{"envelope", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "\[Tau]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1113655915,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 ", the area is ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 ", giving a complete flip for the resonant two-level model above. In our \
truncated five-level model, the drive also transfers amplitude into higher \
levels and back. Amplitude returning to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " has accumulated phase according to those levels\[CloseCurlyQuote] energies \
and interferes with the amplitude already there. This affects the transfer \
between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ", while some population may also remain in higher levels. An area of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " therefore no longer guarantees a complete flip. We calibrate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 ", together with the other pulse controls, rather than fix it at 1."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1606118752,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With the envelope defined, write the Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " for any lowering operator ",
 Cell[BoxData["c"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " can be built for any number of kept levels:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2141499446,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"hamiltonian", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", " ", "@", " ", "c"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Delta]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "c"}], 
      ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"envelope", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"c", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{"envelope", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Alpha]"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "c"}], 
        ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->339082558,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Make ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 " for the five-level oscillator one operator. Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Parameters\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 " list fixes the order in which numbers are supplied later: the \
anharmonicity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 ", the amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 ", the DRAG coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 ", the detuning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 " and the pulse length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->432388834,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"hamiltonian", "[", "b", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "A", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "\[Delta]", 
       ",", " ", "\[Tau]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->443736588,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " and measure time in nanoseconds, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 " are expressed in radians per nanosecond. The amplitude factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " and DRAG coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " are dimensionless. An anharmonicity of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", "200", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["MHz",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 " corresponds to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "=", "-", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[Times]", "0.2", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"rad", "/", "ns"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1593449978,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"anharmonicity", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "Pi", " ", "0.2"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1742646261,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell["Leakage", "Section",
 CellID->29467524,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We now examine how coupling to higher levels affects the transfer of \
population from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 ". Before calibrating the controls, we follow the population during an 8 ns \
pulse of area ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ". Starting from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 ", evolve the transmon with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ", no DRAG (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 ") and no detuning (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1939141443,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"model", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "anharmonicity", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
      "8"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->5047578,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive is resonant with the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"0"},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " transition, while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{"1"},
    "Ket"], "\[Rule]", 
   TemplateBox[{"2"},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " is off resonance by ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],
 ". When ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[LessLess]", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ", excitation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 " is weak. When ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " becomes comparable to ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 ", the drive can transfer substantial population into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 ". We chose a short 8 ns pulse, whose drive is strong, to make this \
excitation visible. For the same pulse shape and area, a longer pulse has a \
weaker drive."
}], "Text",
 CellID->15008895,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the populations of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 " during the pulse, together with the shape of the pulse scaled to a peak of \
1:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1892712309,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"psi", "[", "t", "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", 
        "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{";;", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"envelope", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"envelope", " ", "/.", " ", 
          RowBox[{"t", " ", "->", " ", "4"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"A", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\[Tau]", " ", "->", " ", "8"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "Automatic", ",", " ", "Automatic", ",", " ", "Automatic", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<|0\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<|1\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<|2\[RightAngleBracket]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<pulse shape (scaled)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<population change during a \[Pi] pulse\>\""}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<t (ns)\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<population\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->787969749,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Population reaches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 " through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 ", since the drive couples only neighboring levels. Its population grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " becomes occupied and the drive strengthens. As the drive weakens, some \
population returns to the qubit, but ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 " does not empty completely."
}], "Text",
 CellID->525088789,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell["Compute the populations at the end of the pulse:", "Text",
 CellID->357930410,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "8", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probabilities\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1802489801,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The final population outside ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 " has two contributions: population in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 ", indicating an incomplete flip, and population in higher levels, mainly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],
 ", which is leakage."
}], "Text",
 CellID->115301326,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell["\<\
The short 8 ns pulse makes leakage easy to see. Single-qubit gates on current \
devices last about 25 to 35 ns. The final populations of the same \
uncalibrated \[Pi] pulse lasting 30 ns:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1651187567,ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"model", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "anharmonicity", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
       "30"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "30"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", "30",
    "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probabilities\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->941376513,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Leakage into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " is now small, and most of the error is population left in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 ". While the drive is on, its coupling to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " pushes the energy of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 " up, so the drive falls slightly out of resonance with the qubit and the \
flip stays incomplete. Calibrating the amplitude and detuning of the pulse \
corrects this, and DRAG reduces the leakage. How short a calibrated pulse can \
be is then set by energy decay and dephasing, which we add next."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2120243592,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell["Decoherence and the Best Pulse Length", "Section",
 CellID->1047559317,ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell["\<\
A short pulse leaks, and a long pulse is exposed for longer to energy decay \
and dephasing. The best length balances the two. We therefore include both \
processes and, as on a real device, calibrate the pulse controls with them \
present.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1820947576,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We describe the state by a density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " in our truncated five-level model. Keeping the same Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 ", we include energy decay and pure dephasing through the Lindblad master \
equation:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->670734585,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[Element]", "{", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "}"}]}],
     LimitsPositioning->False], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->58232708,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["The two Lindblad operators, with their rates included, are", "Text",
 CellID->393464600,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
     SqrtBox[
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     SqrtBox[
      FractionBox["2", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["b", "TI"], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1484396876,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first describes energy decay from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 " at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 ". The second describes pure dephasing: on its own, it damps the \
off-diagonal entries of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 " while leaving the populations unchanged. The pure dephasing time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 " is related to the qubit\[CloseCurlyQuote]s energy decay time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " and coherence time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " by"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1149283354,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["1", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]], "=", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"]], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", 
     RowBox[{"2", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1092188694,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For this example, take ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "=", "100", "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s",
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 ". Express both times in nanoseconds:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->559599970,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"T1", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"T2", " ", "=", " ", "100000"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1710123944,ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the corresponding pure dephasing time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 ", also in nanoseconds:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->934597701,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"dephasingTime", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "T2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "T1"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->284780108,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Calibration requires simulating the pulse for many trial settings. We \
therefore construct the Lindblad equation once, keeping the controls and the \
length as parameters, and solve it numerically for each set of values. Set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<ReturnEquations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " to obtain the equation and initial condition for a transmon starting in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 " without solving them. Here ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 " takes the operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " with their rates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "/", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 " supplied separately. The upper limit ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],
 " is a placeholder, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Most"]], "paclet:ref/Most"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],
 " drops the time range, the last of the three results:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->643798763,ExpressionUUID->"3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"openEquations", ",", " ", "openState"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Most", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"model", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "anharmonicity", ",", " ", "A", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
        "\[Delta]", ",", " ", "\[Tau]"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"b", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"b", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "b"}]}], 
        "}"}], " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "T1"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", "/", "dephasingTime"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<ReturnEquations\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->268959046,ExpressionUUID->"0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Represent each entry of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"5", "\[Times]", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " density matrix by a function of time. Substituting this matrix into the \
Lindblad equation gives the coupled equations for its 25 entries. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Normal"]], "paclet:ref/Normal"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " converts the sparse arrays in the equations to ordinary lists:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->403125484,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"densityEntries", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"densityEquations", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", "openEquations", "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"openState", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", "s", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
          "densityEntries", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->931950651,ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define ",
 Cell[BoxData["openSolution"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 ", which substitutes numerical values for the controls and the length into \
these equations and solves them with ",
 Cell[BoxData["NDSolveValue"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 ". For each choice of values, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"openSolution", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", "length"}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 " returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"5", "\[Times]", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],
 " matrix whose entries are functions of time. We raise the precision and \
accuracy goals because the errors computed below are small:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->412518898,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"openSolution", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"amplitude_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"drag_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"detuning_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"length_", "?", "NumericQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"densityEquations", " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A", " ", "->", " ", "amplitude"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "drag"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Delta]", " ", "->", " ", "detuning"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Tau]", " ", "->", " ", "length"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", "densityEntries", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "length"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PrecisionGoal", " ", "->", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"AccuracyGoal", " ", "->", " ", "12"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->622967176,ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the transfer error as one minus the final population in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ", starting from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 ". With the density matrix, this population is the second diagonal entry at \
the end of the pulse. The transfer error follows only the initial state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 "; the full gate is checked below."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1358080856,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"openError", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"amplitude_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"drag_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"detuning_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"length_", "?", "NumericQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"openSolution", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
        "length"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "length", "]"}], 
    "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->320615307,ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To calibrate a pulse of a given length, minimize its transfer error with ",
 Cell[BoxData["NMinimize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 ": over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " without DRAG, and over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],
 " with DRAG. Both searches use the same bounds. We keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "<", 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "<", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 ": reversing the drive's sign leaves the populations unchanged when starting \
from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 ", and below 2 the pulse stays near area ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 ", the \[Pi] pulse studied here. We keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ", about twice the value that cancels leakage to first order anywhere in the \
detuning range searched, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[LessEqual]", "0.5"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " rad/ns. The search uses differential evolution, which improves a \
population of trial pulses; 10 of them keep each search short:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1594238871,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"controls", "[", "True", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"amplitude", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"drag", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"detuning", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "0.5"}], ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"controls", "[", "False", "]"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"amplitude", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"detuning", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "0.5"}], ",", " ", "0.5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bounds", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "amplitude", " ", "<", " ", "2"}], " ", "&&", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "drag", " ", "<=", " ", "3"}], " ", "&&", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "0.5"}], " ", "<=", " ", "detuning", " ", "<=", " ", 
     "0.5"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"calibrate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"withDRAG_", ",", " ", "length_", ",", " ", "seed_"}], "]"}], " ", 
  ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"NMinimize", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"openError", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
         "length"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "bounds"}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"drag", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"controls", "[", "withDRAG", "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<DifferentialEvolution\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<SearchPoints\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<RandomSeed\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "seed"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->2002505366,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Calibrate pulses from 6 to 40 ns, with and without DRAG. Each search starts \
from random trial pulses, so each one is run with two random seeds and the \
lower error is kept; a search that stops early shows up as a disagreement \
between the two. The searches are independent, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ParallelMap"]], "paclet:ref/ParallelMap"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 " runs them on separate kernels:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2121396920,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"lengths", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "24"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"26", ",", " ", "40", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"scan", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ParallelMap", "[", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
          RowBox[{"length", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", 
            RowBox[{"MinimalBy", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"calibrate", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", "length", ",", " ", "#"}], 
                 "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "First"}], 
             "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "lengths", ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<FinestGrained\>\""}]}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"True", ",", " ", "False"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->993357154,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the transfer error of the calibrated pulse at each length:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->50259360,ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"lengths", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"First", " ", "/@", " ", "#"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
    " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", "scan", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<with DRAG\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<without DRAG\>\""}], "}"}]}],
    ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<transfer error of the calibrated pulse\>\""}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<pulse length (ns)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<transfer error\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->680111415,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell["\<\
At short lengths leakage dominates, and the error falls steeply as the pulse \
gets longer. At long lengths both curves rise together, because energy decay \
and dephasing grow with the length while leakage has died out. DRAG lowers \
the error most where leakage dominates, so its curve reaches the rising side \
at a shorter length. Neither curve falls smoothly: leakage passes through \
dips at particular lengths, and the lowest DRAG error sits in a dip narrower \
than the 1 ns spacing of the scan.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1912025938,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell["\<\
Because a dip can be narrower than the spacing of the scan, the lowest \
scanned point need not lie in the deepest dip. Every dip shows up as a \
scanned length whose error is lower than at both neighbors, and the bottom of \
that dip lies between the two neighbors. The windows around the dips of each \
curve:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1678275947,ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"windows", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
     RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"With", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"errors", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"First", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"scan", "[", "withDRAG", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
        "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"lengths", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
          "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Length", "[", "lengths", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}],
             "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"errors", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
              RowBox[{"errors", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"#", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
              "]"}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"True", ",", " ", "False"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1570109414,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell["\<\
In each window, search over the controls and the length together:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->746824257,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bestPulse", "[", 
   RowBox[{"withDRAG_", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"shortest_", ",", " ", "longest_"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "seed_"}], 
   "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"NMinimize", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"openError", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
         "length"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "bounds", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "shortest", " ", "<=", " ", "length", " ", "<=", " ", "longest"}]}], 
      "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"drag", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"controls", "[", "withDRAG", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"length", ",", " ", "shortest", ",", " ", "longest"}], "}"}]}],
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<DifferentialEvolution\>\"", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<RandomSeed\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "seed"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->966663717,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell["\<\
Search every window with two seeds and keep the best pulse with and without \
DRAG:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->634665076,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"bestWithDRAG", ",", " ", "bestWithoutDRAG"}], "}"}], " ", "=", 
  " ", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
     RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"First", "[", 
       RowBox[{"MinimalBy", "[", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ParallelMap", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"bestPulse", "[", 
             RowBox[{"withDRAG", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
           
           RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"windows", "[", "withDRAG", "]"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           
           RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<FinestGrained\>\""}]}], 
          "]"}], ",", "\n", "      ", "First"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"True", ",", " ", "False"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->1607396713,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To see what sets the error of each best pulse, also compute it without \
decay and dephasing. Define the final populations of a transmon truncated to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 " levels, with the same Hamiltonian, solved with ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumEvolve"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 "; with five levels this is the Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger counterpart of ",
 Cell[BoxData["openSolution"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 ". Its precision and accuracy goals are stricter, so the default integration \
method can stop partway through some pulses; an explicit Runge-Kutta method \
is used instead:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->171231949,ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "amplitude_", ",", " ", "drag_", ",", " ", "detuning_", ",", " ", 
      "length_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumEvolve", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"hamiltonian", "[", 
          RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "n", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
           "\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "A", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", 
            "\[Delta]", ",", " ", "\[Tau]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{
       "anharmonicity", ",", " ", "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", 
        "detuning", ",", " ", "length"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "length"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<ExplicitRungeKutta\>\""}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"PrecisionGoal", " ", "->", " ", "12"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"AccuracyGoal", " ", "->", " ", "14"}]}], "]"}], "[", "length", 
    "]"}], "[", "\"\<ProbabilitiesList\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->820919957,ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell["\<\
Compare the two best pulses. For each, the table gives its length, its \
transfer error, the error of the same pulse without decay and dephasing, and \
its controls:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1006830744,ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"summary", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"error_", ",", " ", "rules_"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"pulse", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
         "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
          "length"}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rules", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"drag", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<length (ns)\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<error\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<error without decay and dephasing\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<amplitude\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<DRAG coefficient\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<detuning (MHz)\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"pulse", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "error", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
            RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "pulse"}], "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"pulse", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"pulse", "[", 
          RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1000", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"pulse", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Dataset", "[", 
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<with DRAG\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"summary", "[", "bestWithDRAG", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<without DRAG\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"summary", "[", "bestWithoutDRAG", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}], 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->1175763064,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell["\<\
Without decay and dephasing, the error of each best pulse is far smaller, so \
decay and dephasing set most of it for both pulses. The DRAG pulse reaches \
this limit at less than half the length of the pulse without DRAG, so it is \
exposed to decay and dephasing for less time and ends with the smaller error. \
The price is a stronger drive.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1074416020,ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The transfer error follows only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 ", while the gate must also flip ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],
 " and superpositions. The Hamiltonian at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "-", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],
 " is the transpose of the Hamiltonian at time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],
 ": the DRAG term keeps its form because both ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "."]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " change sign. Without decay and dephasing, the pulse therefore carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],
 " with exactly the same amplitude as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 ", so the flip needs no phase correction to act as an X gate. To check this \
with decay and dephasing included, define the gate error: start from each of \
the six states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
     TemplateBox[{"1"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"0"},
      "Ket"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{"1"},
       "Ket"]}]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],
 ", and average one minus the overlap of the final density matrix with the X \
image of the starting state. The first part of ",
 Cell[BoxData["densityEquations"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 " is the Lindblad equation without its initial condition:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2143439988,ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"finalDensityMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rho0_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "amplitude_", ",", " ", "drag_", ",", " ", "detuning_", ",", " ", 
       "length_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"#", "[", "length", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"NDSolveValue", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"densityEquations", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
             "densityEntries", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "rho0"}]}], 
         "}"}], " ", "/.", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"A", " ", "->", " ", "amplitude"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "drag"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Delta]", " ", "->", " ", "detuning"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Tau]", " ", "->", " ", "length"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", "densityEntries", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "length"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"PrecisionGoal", " ", "->", " ", "10"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"AccuracyGoal", " ", "->", " ", "12"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gateError", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"amplitude_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"drag_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"detuning_", "?", "NumericQ"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"length_", "?", "NumericQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Map", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"in", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
             RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"out", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}]}]}], 
          "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "out", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"finalDensityMatrix", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
              RowBox[{"in", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "in", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
              "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
               "length"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "out"}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"Normalize", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "I"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"-", "I"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->1933756212,ExpressionUUID->"14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],

Cell["The gate errors of the two best pulses:", "Text",
 CellID->943735407,ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<with DRAG\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gateError", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
       "length"}], "]"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "[", "bestWithDRAG", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\"\<without DRAG\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gateError", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "amplitude", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", "length"}], 
      "]"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "[", "bestWithoutDRAG", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->865519937,ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For both pulses the gate error is within a few percent of the transfer \
error, and the DRAG pulse still has the smaller error. Calibrating on the \
transfer from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " therefore gives pulses that are equally good X gates."
}], "Text",
 CellID->845186625,ExpressionUUID->"05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],

Cell["\<\
The pulse without DRAG needs its greater length for leakage to die down. \
Calibrate it instead at the length of the best DRAG pulse:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->14312863,ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dragLength", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"length", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "[", "bestWithDRAG", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"sameLengthWithoutDRAG", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"First", "[", 
   RowBox[{"MinimalBy", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"calibrate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"False", ",", " ", "dragLength", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", 
       "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", "First"}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->315698450,ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell["\<\
Solve both pulses of this length, the best DRAG pulse and the pulse without \
DRAG just calibrated:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1751204118,ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rhoDRAG", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"openSolution", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
      "dragLength"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "[", "bestWithDRAG", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rhoWithoutDRAG", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"openSolution", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "amplitude", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
      "dragLength"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Last", "[", "sameLengthWithoutDRAG", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->2116603297,ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the population of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 " during the two pulses. A logarithmic vertical scale makes the small \
populations remaining at the end easier to compare:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->530919167,ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"LogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"rhoWithoutDRAG", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "t", "]"}], ",", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"rhoDRAG", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}],
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "dragLength"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "3", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<|2\[RightAngleBracket] no DRAG\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<|2\[RightAngleBracket] DRAG\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<leakage during pulses of the same length\>\""}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<t (ns)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<population of |2\[RightAngleBracket]\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->1242319925,ExpressionUUID->"114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The population the pulse without DRAG leaves in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1600082692,ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rhoWithoutDRAG", "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "dragLength", "]"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1091979148,ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At the same length, the pulse without DRAG has a much larger error than the \
DRAG pulse, and almost all the population that misses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],
 " ends up in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],
 ": its error is leakage. DRAG removes this leakage, which is why the DRAG \
pulse can be this short."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1239660989,ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],

Cell["Five Levels Are Enough", "Section",
 CellID->234435634,ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every result above keeps five levels. The smallest error in this tutorial \
is that of the best DRAG pulse without decay and dephasing, where a change \
from the truncation would matter most. Its transfer error with five and with \
six levels, using ",
 Cell[BoxData["finalPopulations"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],
 " defined above:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->417968184,ExpressionUUID->"1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"finalPopulations", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "amplitude", ",", " ", "drag", ",", " ", "detuning", ",", " ", 
           "length"}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Last", "[", "bestWithDRAG", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->1274591649,ExpressionUUID->"604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A sixth level changes this error by well under a percent, so the levels \
above ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"4"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 " do not affect the results."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1243964799,ExpressionUUID->"635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],

